{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MLNOverlay","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" <","kind":"text"},{"text":"MLNAnnotation","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(pl)MLNAnnotation","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You use overlays to layer more sophisticated content on top of a map view. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, you could use an overlay to show the boundaries of a national park or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace a bus route along city streets. This SDK defines several concrete classes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that conform to this protocol and define standard shapes.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnoverlay"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MLNOverlay","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"c:objc(pl)MLNOverlay","title":"MLNOverlay","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"fragments":[{"text":"MLNOverlay","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay"},{"text":" protocol defines a specific type of annotation that represents","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both a point and an area on a map. Overlay objects are essentially data objects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that contain the geographic data needed to represent the map area. Overlays can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take the form of a polyline or polygon.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation"],"type":"inheritsFrom"},{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPointCollection","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline"],"type":"conformingTypes"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/coordinate","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/overlayBounds"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/intersectsOverlayBounds:"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNMultiPolygon":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polygons that do not overlap. For example, you could use a multipolygon shape","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to represent the body of land that consists of an island surrounded by an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"atoll: the inner island would be one ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"text":" object, while the surrounding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"atoll would be another. You could also use a multipolygon shape to represent a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group of disconnected but related buildings.","type":"text"}],"title":"MLNMultiPolygon","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnmultipolygon","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon","fragments":[{"text":"MLNMultiPolygon","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"text":" object represents a closed shape consisting of four or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, specified as ","type":"text"},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances, and the edges that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connect them. For example, you could use a polygon shape to represent a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"building, a lake, or an area you want to highlight.","type":"text"}],"title":"MLNPolygon","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolygon","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling.","type":"text"}],"title":"MapLibre","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPointCollection":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPointCollection"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disconnected vertices, specified as ","type":"text"},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"points in the collection may be related but are not connected spatially. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, you could use a point collection to represent all the trees in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orchard.","type":"text"}],"title":"MLNPointCollection","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpointcollection","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPointCollection","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPointCollection","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNAnnotation":{"type":"topic","title":"MLNAnnotation","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol is used to provide annotation-related information","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to a map view. To use this protocol, you adopt it in any custom objects that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store or represent annotation data. Each object then serves as the source of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information about a single map annotation and provides critical information,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as the annotation’s location on the map. Annotation objects do not provide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the visual representation of the annotation but typically coordinate (in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjunction with the map view’s delegate) the creation of an appropriate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"objects to handle the display.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnannotation","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNAnnotation"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolyline":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of two or more vertices,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified as ","type":"text"},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances, and the line segments that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connect them. For example, you could use an polyline to represent a road or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path along which something moves.","type":"text"}],"title":"MLNPolyline","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolyline","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolyline","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNOverlay":{"title":"MLNOverlay","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNOverlay"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay"},{"text":" protocol defines a specific type of annotation that represents","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both a point and an area on a map. Overlay objects are essentially data objects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that contain the geographic data needed to represent the map area. Overlays can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take the form of a polyline or polygon.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnoverlay","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNOverlay/intersectsOverlayBounds:":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Returns a Boolean indicating whether the specified rectangle intersects the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"receiver’s shape."}],"title":"intersectsOverlayBounds:","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnoverlay\/intersectsoverlaybounds:","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/intersectsOverlayBounds:","fragments":[{"text":"- ","kind":"text"},{"text":"intersectsOverlayBounds:","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNOverlay/coordinate":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A coordinate representing the overlay. (required) (read-only)"}],"title":"coordinate","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnoverlay\/coordinate","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/coordinate","fragments":[{"text":"coordinate","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNMultiPolyline":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polylines. For example, you could use a multipolyline shape to represent both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a divided highway (dual carriageway), excluding the median (central","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reservation): each carriageway would be a distinct ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}],"title":"MLNMultiPolyline","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnmultipolyline","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline","fragments":[{"text":"MLNMultiPolyline","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNOverlay/overlayBounds":{"fragments":[{"text":"overlayBounds","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNOverlay\/overlayBounds","title":"overlayBounds","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnoverlay\/overlaybounds","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The cooordinate rectangle that encompasses the overlay. (required) (read-only)"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}